Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Riemannian Infrageometry", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Riemannian Infrageometry",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " measures and distinguishes graphs as geometric substrates. In contrast, \
synthetic infrageometry asks only whether certain postulates are satisfied by \
the substrate so that its propositions about geometric objects hold. Riemann \
viewed space as an ",
 StyleBox["infinitesimal webbing of paths",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and, by imposing conditions on the infinitesimal length element, arrived \
at the quadratic metric tensor as the lowest-order data satisfying those \
conditions. This separates the manifold from the Riemannian structure, so one \
can ask for the moduli space of Riemannian structures on a fixed manifold, or \
go the other way and obtain topological quantities from Riemannian ones. In \
infrageometry, the ",
 StyleBox["discrete webbing of paths",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " given by a graph is the geometric substrate itself, and no such split \
occurs. We relate it to infinitesimal geometry through rescaled \
Gromov\[Dash]Hausdorff convergence, where the scaling is determined by the ",
 StyleBox["observer's scale",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", offering an alternative approach to geometry: if a limit of rescaled \
graphs yields a metric space arising from a Riemannian manifold, then that \
manifold is uniquely determined up to isomorphism."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "GuideFunctionsSection",
 CellID->1866139230,ExpressionUUID->"a0ea3657-4c83-4862-93c8-ecf80cebc774"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A geodesic at observer scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c8ea8ba-3a81-419f-8834-bcf1ac047e49"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraGeodesic", "[",
   RowBox[{"germ", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c766b45f-1379-4771-bd9f-5d9b603758ec"],
 ", is a family of walks that are shortest paths in every window of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e10f69df-637e-4f40-9a93-aa1019101f55"],
 " edges. A representative can be found with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"RandomInfraGeodesic", "[", "...", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e6325cd-7312-41ab-80c2-1d2a819f279e"],
 ", and its edge density with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraMeasurement", "[",
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "geodesic", ",", " ", "\"\<EdgeDensity\>\""}],
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b58e2907-bc9e-4985-81bd-dead6c6e5ab8"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"819597ca-172c-47ca-908e-9eb9ae1887ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can measure the volumes of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraBall", "[",
   RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "r0"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83be27eb-59e4-489a-a689-cc06ac5be929"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"r0", " ", "<=", " ", "r"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f552c7fb-eb34-4d54-8542-85dd10ef8ad0"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraTube", "[",
   RowBox[{"axis", ",", " ", "s"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b62bf06-85e8-4639-9efd-fd9fa7368c09"],
 " for any ray or line through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f713cb9-b758-4798-b565-db25061a9d27"],
 " and any thickness ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c079104c-8ca2-4aff-b3f5-9a2371f1b78f"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraCone", "[",
   RowBox[{"axis", ",", " ", "s"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45153885-a067-479c-8ee1-6f111dbfcbd7"],
 " for slope ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "94af52c4-9666-4828-aad0-9df9bf83bfe7"],
 ". Such measurements have asymptotic expansions in the continuous case and \
can be used to determine limiting curvature components. However, no sphere \
structure exists a priori on ",
 Cell[BoxData["InfraShell"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a0d63af1-a80d-46f2-a310-51d30c0530c6"],
 ", so the limiting linear tensors can be compared only through histograms. \
We can also obtain the histogram of mutual distances between points, which \
constrains the limiting Riemannian manifold."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"ee048666-aeb0-411b-b305-db9918b5a446"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraTangentBundle", "[",
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a1be97-a90b-41a9-8ee4-f1f4ac7d5493"],
 " which represents vectors at p by rays of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fcf0c57a-e9ab-48d3-87d1-d32f8da93a81"],
 ", and these are compactly encoded as chains in the spray graph at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ef90102-b617-462c-9512-0846dd744af1"],
 ". We have an even simpler infra-bundle, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[",
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "623c0226-45ac-4eae-a3e0-0afdb7c835ad"],
 ", that keeps only the endpoints of rays. We have a minimal model of the \
Levi-Civita connection, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"FindInfraLeviCivitaConnection", "[",
   RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[",
    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93cb0cc4-1150-4b98-8101-904c719bb837"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraParallelTransport", "[",
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[",
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "walk"}], "]"}]],
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9b6e9593-238e-40e9-a7eb-9adb1d500f8e"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"2535c6d0-4478-4daf-9fb2-3589ea1bd828"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We also have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraMetricTensor", "[",
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "p", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49073ddb-3940-4bb2-89b3-2ace83ea23d5"],
 ", which computes shortest path projections of rays, displacement commutator \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"DisplacementCommutator", "[",
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "d1", ",", " ", "d2"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c866f6ed-5851-42a0-ae36-94000b78198e"],
 ", and addition of displacements via midpoints with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"DisplacementSum", "[",
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "d1", ",", " ", "d2"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ad5ad504-a00b-48c0-9614-fb7324b03d84"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"2db4cee4-c07b-4c00-8273-4720b2d7c5b8"],

Cell["\t", "GuideDelimiter",ExpressionUUID->"3b670b17-c5d7-4517-b9a6-7761c6b57ab0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Infrageodesics", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"84d098c7-fcd8-48b8-a927-f7021fe72346"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraGeodesic"]],
