 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the \"CountingMeasure\" and the \"RiemannianMeasure\" of a ball, shell or \
tube; the profiles are its Table over the radius"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"7d3dc031-d212-473b-a7cc-517a94e86ec0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A region on a graph is measured by counting vertices, and its boundary is \
not negligible at a finite scale: the vertices at distance exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ae42c76-cf9c-43d2-b266-d30bbd70fb6a"],
 " are a share of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/",
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00ce046d-e1cd-480d-9913-9467acec0998"],
 " of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e293174-828b-4298-b9cb-1cf7517b08f7"],
 ". So every region carries two measures. The counting measure is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"],
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1],
     StyleBox["A", "TI"],
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=",
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["A", "TI"]},
    "Abs"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "206ff0e4-a285-4ec0-802b-f9c45590f665"],
 ". The Riemannian measure is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"],
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1],
     StyleBox["A", "TI"],
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=",
   TemplateBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"]},
    "Abs"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8a0ce3c9-2360-4919-b2d9-e4b4c7bc1c93"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"], "=", "{",
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "\[Element]",
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], ":",
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["N", "TI"],
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1],
    StyleBox["v", "TI"],
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[SubsetEqual]",
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20c25f03-baf3-45c9-bff1-4725639233ea"],
 " is the set of vertices all of whose neighbours lie in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77afb28e-8ed3-4188-a9b4-ab397cba3702"],
 "; it is the count without the boundary and the default of the growth \
estimators."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"95ff8e8a-c8ff-4841-bced-1614e9dd910a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the square grid the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b1d4d07b-2b67-432d-b286-35e602b4608e"],
 " has counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2",
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "+", "2",
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c5e95b1-5174-4b49-9607-db212521a21e"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2",
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "-", "2",
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03f353bf-a789-40e1-96d9-be10eb82ab50"],
 ", the counting measure of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76c33014-f34d-4408-b92d-88811d6634f7"],
 "; the shell has counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4",
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b3cfe4a8-253b-4d8c-a274-fb71ed387b32"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ad6816eb-30e6-4fc8-86ad-8b5434785c27"],
 ". The same shift holds on the triangular lattice before the rim, the \
convention of the Wolfram Physics technical introduction."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"1a6534e1-831b-41b9-9f48-5f2713fdba58"],

